(6165615, 909625, 83149, '<td valign="top">I thought, what the hell is it, then my 9 year old daughter who was looking over my shoulder said, "cool, a drop of water on a spider web".  Then I thought, she''s right, and it is pretty cool.  It would be better I think without the drop cropped and a little deeper depth of field (I might have known what it was then).  Still pretty nice though.</td>', 'I thought, what the hell is it, then my 9 year old daughter who was looking over my shoulder said, "cool, a drop of water on a spider web".  Then I thought, she''s right, and it is pretty cool.  It would be better I think without the drop cropped and a little deeper depth of field (I might have known what it was then).  Still pretty nice though.', '2010-09-18 20:15:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6165630, 908877, 81362, '<td valign="top">When I scroll to hide the bright yellow-green area on the right, the remaining image beocmes much stronger and seems much more interesting.</td>', 'When I scroll to hide the bright yellow-green area on the right, the remaining image beocmes much stronger and seems much more interesting.', '2010-09-18 20:26:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6165636, 908917, 81362, '<td valign="top">Cozy sensation, good catch and title. Difficult to reconcile exposure with challenge topic.</td>', 'Cozy sensation, good catch and title. Difficult to reconcile exposure with challenge topic.', '2010-09-18 20:28:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6165677, 908544, 54778, '<td valign="top">The exposure''s perfectly okay.. which might pose a problem in this challenge</td>', 'The exposure''s perfectly okay.. which might pose a problem in this challenge', '2010-09-18 22:07:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6165757, 908636, 30364, '<td valign="top">It''s actually beautifully exposed, and not underexposed. Any more light than this and the picture was lost (unless one resorted to one of those HDR abominations, in which case it''s the photographer that would be lost).  Photographs of consequence are rarely about detail, rarely about what''s said: it''s what''s <i>not</i> said that gives them voice.  Just like this.  Top two pick from me.</td>', 'It''s actually beautifully exposed, and not underexposed. Any more light than this and the picture was lost (unless one resorted to one of those HDR abominations, in which case it''s the photographer that would be lost).  Photographs of consequence are rarely about detail, rarely about what''s said: it''s what''s not said that gives them voice.  Just like this.  Top two pick from me.', '2010-09-19 03:17:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6165759, 909452, 30364, '<td valign="top">Ambiguity, teetering on the edge of obscurity.  I like that!  Thanks.</td>', 'Ambiguity, teetering on the edge of obscurity.  I like that!  Thanks.', '2010-09-19 03:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
