(6169336, 909595, 22689, '<td valign="top">After reading the comment left by Paul (<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30364" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">ubique</a>), there''s little to add.<br/>It''s really a wonderful photo, the atmosphere is quiet and serene and the swan adds the touch of magic.</td>', 'After reading the comment left by Paul ( ubique), there''s little to add.It''s really a wonderful photo, the atmosphere is quiet and serene and the swan adds the touch of magic.', '2010-09-22 12:11:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6169400, 908552, 106806, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wyverndragon:</b></div><hr/><i> I have a hard time thinking of this as underexposed, as the majority of the pixels are in the top half of the histogram.  Absolutely stunning image though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Kinda agree in a way (there is no kinda about the stunning ... it is stunning FACT) ... this is a pretty paradoxical image under and over (ok well) exposed at the same time awsome and a worthy ribboner in my view.</td>', 'Originally posted by wyverndragon: I have a hard time thinking of this as underexposed, as the majority of the pixels are in the top half of the histogram.  Absolutely stunning image though.   Kinda agree in a way (there is no kinda about the stunning ... it is stunning FACT) ... this is a pretty paradoxical image under and over (ok well) exposed at the same time awsome and a worthy ribboner in my view.', '2010-09-22 13:02:55.000000', NULL, 0),
