(6267015, 908891, 113956, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by FrankRobinson:</b></div><hr/><i> Finally - real use of underexposure to add effect! Fine work. The only downside is the tilted rear horizon. I am not convinced that the top two inches add anything - maybe they could have just been cropped off? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you''re right!</td>', 'Originally posted by FrankRobinson: Finally - real use of underexposure to add effect! Fine work. The only downside is the tilted rear horizon. I am not convinced that the top two inches add anything - maybe they could have just been cropped off?   you''re right!', '2011-01-02 08:21:46.000000', NULL, 0),
